<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hanwant Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1923">1923</a>–<a href="/years/1952">1952</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Hanwant Singh of Jodhpur</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hanwant Singh was the last ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a>, succeeding in 1947. At independence he briefly considered acceding to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> before signing the accession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and in 1949 his state merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>. He entered electoral politics and was killed in an air crash in January 1952, during the first Indian general election.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hanwant-singh.jpg" alt="Hanwant Singh" width="250" height="340" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hanwant_Singh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
